## 3. Real-World Post-Mortems & Incident References

The static pod failure modes practiced in this lab directly model documented, high-impact production outages:

- **Monzo Bank (2018)**:
  - *Outage*: Banking deployment stall caused by an invalid credential path in scheduler kubeconfig.
  - *Drill Mapping*: **Scenario 1** (Broken Kubeconfig Path).
  - *Reference*: [hjacobs/kubernetes-failure-stories #15](https://github.com/hjacobs/kubernetes-failure-stories)
- **Target Corporation (2019)**:
  - *Outage*: Node OS upgrade desynchronized HostPath volume mount for PKI credentials.
  - *Drill Mapping*: **Scenario 2** (HostPath Mount Drift).
  - *Reference*: [Target Kubernetes Retrospective](https://github.com/hjacobs/kubernetes-failure-stories)
- **Datadog (2020)**:
  - *Outage*: Scheduler leader election drops and crashloops from client endpoint drift.
  - *Drill Mapping*: **Scenario 4** (Server Endpoint Drift).
  - *Reference*: [Datadog K8s Scheduling Post-Mortem](https://github.com/hjacobs/kubernetes-failure-stories)
- **OpenAI (2021)**:
  - *Outage*: Silent static pod watcher drops during in-place atomic file replacements (`sed -i`).
  - *Drill Mapping*: Script analysis and inode watch gotchas.
  - *Reference*: [OpenAI 7,500 Nodes Post-Mortem](https://openai.com/index/scaling-kubernetes-to-7500-nodes/)
- **Kubernetes SIG-Node**:
  - *Outage*: Kubelet removes mirror pods on YAML parse errors instead of reporting `Error`.
  - *Drill Mapping*: **Scenario 3** (YAML Syntax Error).
  - *Reference*: [Kubernetes Issue #65454](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/65454)
- **CNCF / Linux Foundation**:
  - *Competency*: Standard certification competencies for control plane static pod recovery.
  - *Drill Mapping*: Exam curriculum objectives.
  - *Reference*: [CNCF CKA Curriculum](https://github.com/cncf/curriculum)
